  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>z</mi></mfenced></math> represent the principal argument of the complex number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>.</p><p>The, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;will represent a circle with centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>units</mtext></math></p><p>And&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>arg</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>arg</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;will represent arc of the circle with centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>, now on plotting the diagram,</p><p>&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/174fea64-68f2-48c7-8ff4-79db2e59c81a-image.png\" style=\"width: 241px; height: 200px;\" />&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>We can see they are intersecting nowhere.</p>",
